  "dictionary": {
    "factorDescriptions": {
      "node-1778064957787": "Higher dependence increases vulnerability to access loss (https://marketac.eu/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/Item-7-Overview-study-of-the-effects-of-offshore-wind-on-fisheries-and-aquaculture.pdf)\n",
      "node-1778065188507": "Passive gears may benefit where access is allowed (https://tethys.pnnl.gov/sites/default/files/publications/Svendsen-et-al-2022.pdf)",
      "node-1778070886335": "OWF exclusion zones create de facto sheltered areas suitable for aquaculture deployment. (https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2026.1739325/full)\nWave shadowing and reduced extreme exposure influence aquaculture system stability.\nAquaculture Co‑location Presence → Fisheries–Aquaculture Conflict (–)\nOnly when participatory planning and access‑sharing are implemented. (https://tethys.pnnl.gov/publications/offshore-wind-aquaculture-co-location-challenges-opportunities-us-federal-waters)\nAquaculture Co‑location Presence → IF Effort Redistribution Capacity (0)\nLimited interaction; IF rarely integrates with aquaculture operations (https://maritime-spatial-planning.ec.europa.eu/practices/overview-effects-offshore-wind-farms-fisheries-and-aquaculture)\n",
      "node-1778071199217": "Positive for seaweed and bivalves; uncertain for finfish cages. (https://www.nature.com/articles/s43247-023-01116-6)"
    },
    "connectionJustifications": {
      "link-1776845658020": {
        "control": "Construction & O&M increase traffic; mitigation possible but not eliminable"
      }
    }
  },
